==Battleground==
*1 [[Cyberhorn]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*10 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**8 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn, delay 8.33~10 seconds<sup>250f~300f</sup>.
**4 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns.

==Strategy==
One way of beating this stage is to use the Cyberhorn at the beginning to stack [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] cats such as [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] to snipe the enemy base and the Corporal Weylands, and/or units that can help in dealing with the Oldhorns like [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ultra Delinquent Cat]] and/or [[Talents|talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]].

In higher crowned difficulties, Idi:NX and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] are a fun and effective choice to re-beat this stage. The former can abuse Corporal Weyland's Warps to repeatedly score hits on the Oldhorns,  and the latter is Immune to Warp, letting him go bananas on the battlefield without interruption.

